    "result_text": "All 263 tests pass \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**, including the new `AcceptanceTest.coreDerivesAgeBand`. (The stack trace earlier in the log was a test exercising an error path; the summary confirms 0 failures/0 errors.)\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `birthDate` \u2192 `ageBand` feature on the owner endpoint. Since the request/response DTOs are generated from `openapi.yml` at build time, the change spans the spec, the entity, the DB schemas, and the mapper:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`**\n   - Added `birthDate` (optional, `format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` input schema.\n   - Added `ageBand` (readOnly string) to the `Owner` output schema, kept as a plain string to match the existing derived fields (`locality`, `contactPreference`).\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `birthDate` (`birth_date`) `LocalDate` field with getter/setter. MapStruct maps it in and out by name automatically.\n\n3. **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added a `birth_date DATE` column to `owners` (tests run on hsqldb).\n\n4. **`mapper/AgeBand.java`** (new) \u2014 computes the band via `Period.between(birthDate, registrationDate).getYears()`: `< 18` \u2192 `MINOR`, `18\u201364` \u2192 `ADULT`, `\u2265 65` \u2192 `SENIOR`; returns `null` (field omitted) when no birth date is present. Kept out of `OwnerMapper` so MapStruct doesn't treat it as an implicit mapping method, matching the existing `OwnerLocality` pattern.\n\n5. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 wired `ageBand` to the helper, computed against the owner's `registrationDate` (which the controller already defaults/adjusts before mapping), so it's correct on both create and `GET`.\n\nThe band is computed against `registrationDate` per the spec, and is absent when `birthDate` isn't supplied.",
